# The Vercel CLI uploads from the invoked directory (repo root, since our Vercel project's Root
# Directory setting is apps/dashboard and the CLI must be run from root — see .vercel/README and
# apps/dashboard/vercel.json). It does not reliably honor nested/deep .gitignore rules the way git
# itself does, so a huge, otherwise-git-ignored directory like PebloBuddy/ (a full React Native
# test app with Android build artifacts) still gets bundled unless explicitly listed here — that's
# exactly what caused "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)" / multi-GB upload aborts.
#
# Safe to exclude wholesale: PebloBuddy/ is NOT a pnpm workspace member (pnpm-workspace.yaml only
# globs apps/*, packages/*, examples/*), so pnpm install --frozen-lockfile never needs it present.

# Not a pnpm workspace member — huge Android RN test app, never needed to build the dashboard.
/PebloBuddy/

# Reinstalled fresh via vercel.json's installCommand — never upload existing node_modules.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Android/Gradle build output: pure binary artifacts (APKs, native .so libs, CMake/.cxx caches),
# never part of any package.json pnpm needs to resolve the workspace lockfile.
**/android/**/build/
**/android/**/.cxx/
**/android/**/.gradle/
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.so

# SQLite runtime files (the multi-tenant server DB) — never relevant to a static/Next.js deploy.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# Build caches — regenerated fresh by vercel.json's buildCommand.
**/.next/
**/dist/
.turbo
**/.turbo/

.git
.vscode
.idea
